    "raw": "Given the problem, I have the following quantities:\n- Ground beef is sold in 5-pound packages.\n- Maurice buys 4 packages of ground beef.\n- Each burger requires 2 pounds of ground beef.\n- Maurice wants to make one 2-pound burger for each person, including himself.\n\nFirst, I calculate the total amount of ground beef Maurice has:\n\\[ 4 \\text{ packages} \\times 5 \\text{ pounds/package} = 20 \\text{ pounds} \\]\n\nNext, I determine how many 2-pound burgers can be made from 20 pounds of ground beef:\n\\[ \\frac{20 \\text{ pounds}}{2 \\text{ pounds/burger}} = 10 \\text{ burgers} \\]\n\nSince Maurice wants one burger for each person, including himself, the number of people he can invite is:\n\\[ 10 \\text{ burgers} - 1 \\text{ (Maurice himself)} = 9 \\text{ people} \\]\n\nThus, Maurice can invite 9 people to the cookout.\n\nFINAL: 9",
